On Mon, Jun 15, 2009 at 5:55 AM, tijlan<jbotijlan@gmail.com> wrote:
> What is the correct place number of "da" in "broda da fe de"?
> According to jbofi'e, it's x3. But I think it's x2.
>
 It's x3.  jbofi'e is wrong.

  This thread is interesting, though, because just yesterday, I was
asking in #lojban why jbofi'e wouldn't accept "mi mitre li re to gutci
li xapimuxa toi"* without a lo'o after re.  I guess I should have read
this thread first, because it would have explained it.

*Okay, the actual sentence which had brought it to my attention was
the following from a letter I was writing:
".i .i'u mi kulmu'o la.uupis. lo samske de'i li pasobibi
[lo'o] to co'a lo nu mi velcu'e kei mi me la'e li pasobivo klesi .iku'i
fau lo nungu'a jo'u nuncli pu'u velcu'e kei kuce'o lo nu mi pare'u
fliba la'o .uupis. IQP .uupis. joi la'o .uupis MQP .uupis. kei lo nu
go'i cu co'e to ku'i mi traji snada le remei lo remoi toi toi "

But I thought it better not to complicate things, so I traced down the
actual part that was causing jbofi'e to throw up, and just ask it on
the basic structure.

